            <ArticleTitle>Aspirin sensitivity and the nose.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>442-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There is a well-recognized association of aspirin sensitivity, aspirin-induced asthma, nasal polyposis or sinusitis, known as Samter's triad. This article outlines the pathogenesis and clinical features of this condition and reviews current management options.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
